+# Retry-credit reservation contract
+
+This is an internal service contract. Exact transport, method, and schema names
+belong to the target implementation repository, but all implementations must
+preserve the commands, results, and invariants below.
+
+## Reserve a credit
+
+**Input**
+
+| Field | Required | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | Yes | Identifies the quota owner. |
+| `attempt_id` | Yes | Stable id for the send attempt; idempotency key within the workspace. |
+
+**Behavior**
+
+- Atomically create or return the reservation for the idempotency key.
+- A new reservation may be created only if one credit can be conditionally
+  reserved without making the balance negative.
+- A repeated reserve for an existing `reserved` reservation returns that same
+  reservation and has no second balance effect.
+- A repeated reserve for a terminal reservation returns its terminal state and
+  has no balance effect.
+
+**Result**
+
+| Result | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `reserved` | The caller may dispatch the provider send. |
+| `quota_exhausted` | No credit was reserved; the caller must not dispatch. |
+| `terminal` | The attempt was already finalized or released; no new dispatch or balance change. |
+
+## Record a provider outcome
+
+**Input**
+
+| Field | Required | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | Yes | Must match the reservation scope. |
+| `attempt_id` | Yes | Selects exactly one reservation in the workspace. |
+| `outcome` | Yes | One of `accepted`, `failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled`. |
+
+**Behavior**
+
+| Reservation state | Outcome | Result | Balance effect |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| reserved | accepted | finalized | none |
+| reserved | failed, timed_out, cancelled | released | add one credit |
+| finalized | accepted again | duplicate | none |
+| released | same non-accepted outcome again | duplicate | none |
+| terminal | conflicting outcome | conflict | none |
+| missing | any | not_found | none |
+
+The transition and any release credit must commit atomically. A duplicate,
+conflict, or missing reservation must never cause a balance mutation.
+
+## Contract assertions
+
+- The implementation rejects unrecognized outcomes and incomplete identities.
+- `workspace_id` plus `attempt_id` is unique.
+- The provider dispatch path runs only after receiving `reserved`.
+- A callback is safe to deliver repeatedly and out of order after the first
+  terminal transition.
