+# S004 data model: provider retry quota
+
+## Entities
+
+### WorkspaceRetryQuota
+
+The workspace-scoped source of available retry credits.
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace owner | Primary key or unique scope key. |
+| `available_credits` | Credits that may be reserved | Non-negative integer. |
+| `updated_at` | Last committed change | Updated in the same transaction as a balance mutation. |
+
+### RetryCreditReservation
+
+The durable record that makes an attempt's quota effect idempotent.
+
+| Field | Meaning | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| `reservation_id` | Internal identity | Immutable unique identifier. |
+| `workspace_id` | Workspace whose quota is affected | Must match the quota row. |
+| `attempt_id` | Durable provider-send correlation id | Unique together with `workspace_id`. |
+| `state` | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `released` | Starts as `reserved`; terminal thereafter. |
+| `created_at` | Reservation time | Immutable. |
+| `terminal_at` | Finalization or release time | Present only in terminal states. |
+| `terminal_reason` | Provider outcome for a terminal transition | Required for `released`; `accepted` for `finalized`. |
+
+### ReminderSendAttempt
+
+An existing or target-repository send-attempt record. This story requires only a
+stable `attempt_id` and workspace association; it does not prescribe its wider
+schema.
+
+## Relationships
+
+```text
+WorkspaceRetryQuota (1) ── workspace_id ── (*) RetryCreditReservation
+ReminderSendAttempt (1) ── attempt_id ──── (1) RetryCreditReservation
+```
+
+## State transitions
+
+| Current state | Event | Next state | Balance effect |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| none | reserve with `available_credits > 0` | reserved | subtract 1 |
+| reserved | provider accepted | finalized | none |
+| reserved | provider failed | released | add 1 |
+| reserved | provider timed out | released | add 1 |
+| reserved | operation cancelled | released | add 1 |
+| finalized | duplicate accepted callback | finalized | none |
+| released | duplicate non-accepted callback | released | none |
+
+Conflicting terminal callbacks are not allowed to alter either a terminal
+reservation or the balance. The target repository may record or surface that
+conflict, but it must preserve this invariant.
+
+## Transaction rules
+
+1. Reserve: conditionally decrement a workspace quota with positive available
+   credit and create the `reserved` reservation in the same transaction.
+2. Finalize: transition only `reserved` to `finalized` in one transaction.
+3. Release: transition only `reserved` to `released` and increment the same
+   workspace quota in one transaction.
+4. Rollback: if any statement in a transaction fails, commit neither the
+   reservation transition nor its balance mutation.
+
+## Invariants
+
+- `available_credits >= 0` after every committed transaction.
+- At most one reservation exists for a workspace plus attempt id.
+- A reservation has at most one terminal transition.
+- A credit is consumed only by a finalized accepted send.
+- Every released reservation restores exactly one credit.
